# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, git's `core.autocrlf=true` (a common Windows
# default) checks this repository out with CRLF, while the published npm
# tarball and every CI checkout use LF. Two shipped code paths parse files with
# an exact LF guard, so the CRLF checkout silently took a different branch:
#
#   * index.js:30  — `text.startsWith('---\n')` failed, so the skill registered
#                    its generic fallback description instead of the 355-char
#                    trigger-phrase description from SKILL.md frontmatter, and
#                    registered the raw file (frontmatter included) as the body.
#   * src/cli/commands/check.ts:487 — the same guard failed, so the SKILL.md
#                    frontmatter was never stripped and `redline-persona-role`
#                    judged the `name:` line as the opening paragraph, emitting a
#                    false warning on every local run.
#
# The published artifact escaped both only because release.yml builds in CI.
# Pinning `eol=lf` here makes the checkout match the artifact. The parsers are
# additionally CRLF-tolerant as defence in depth; this file removes the class of
# bug rather than one instance of it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary

# Windows tooling that legitimately needs CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Note: scripts/*.ps1 must ALSO keep a UTF-8 BOM. Per references/sources.md:124
# that is the repository convention, because PowerShell 5.1 decodes a BOM-less
# script as ANSI and the Chinese comments then break the parser - which is
# exactly what had happened to verify-kit.ps1 (5 parse errors at HEAD, silently
# hidden because CI runs it under pwsh). `eol` does not affect the BOM, but do
# not let a linter strip it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Lockfiles and generated artifacts: keep them byte-stable.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf
llms-full.txt text eol=lf
